course: dictionary
lesson: 10270
title: What is the topic?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A topic is the subject that people talk, write or learn about. To find it, ask yourself: what is this about? For a project, you might find facts with the library catalogue, non-fiction books and their index.
explain: In school, a topic is a theme the class studies for some weeks, such as «Space» or «The Romans». A topic can link work in many subjects, so a Space topic could bring in science, maths and writing.
explain: Writers use topic words too. A topic sentence tells the main idea of a paragraph. A report gives facts about a topic, grouped by idea rather than by time.
explain: In everyday talk, «change the topic» means start talking about something else, and «off topic» means not about the main subject. If you are asked to write about rivers and you write about trains, you are off topic.
fact: A topic is the subject that people talk, write or learn about.
fact: In school, a topic is a theme the class studies for some weeks, such as «Space» or «The Romans».
fact: A topic sentence tells the main idea of a paragraph.
fact: «Change the topic» means start talking about something else.
fact: «Off topic» means not about the main subject; «on topic» means about it.
exercise: «A report gives facts about a topic, grouped by idea rather than by time.» What is a topic here? | The number of pages in the report | *The subject the report is about | The date the report was written | The name of the person who wrote it
exercise: Mia says, «We are off topic.» What does she mean? | We have finished our work | *We are talking about something other than the main subject | We are changing the classroom | We are talking about the main subject
exercise: «Repeating a key word, or a synonym for it, helps link paragraphs about the same topic.» What helps link paragraphs? | Writing everything in capital letters | Using a longer title | Adding a picture to each page | *Repeating a key word or a synonym
test: What does a topic sentence do? | It ends a story with a surprise | It lists the pages of a book | *It tells the main idea of a paragraph | It counts the words in a paragraph
test: Ben says, «Let's change the topic.» What does he want? | To stop talking for ever | To read the same page again | *To start talking about something else | To find the index at the back
exam: Which of these is a school topic? | A pencil case | *Space, a theme the class studies for some weeks | A bus timetable | A tin of beans
